    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0679" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg571"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure A.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tracy to commanding officer of the
                    Thetis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-06-15"><hi rendition="#italic">June 15,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Commanding Officer U. S. S.
                        Thetis</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San Francisco, Cal.:</hi></p>
                <p>Proclamation of President closing Behring Sea has been telegraphed to collector
                    of port of San Francisco. Make immediate application for copies as soon as
                    received; proceed with <hi rendition="#italic">Thetis</hi> to Sand Point, Popof
                    Island; distribute the proclamation among the sealing vessels. Warn master of
                    each vessel to whom you may deliver proclamation that name of vessel has been
                    taken, and that vessel will be liable to capture if found to have been or to be
                    sealing in Behring Sea east of line of demarcation after <pb facs="0680" n="572"
                        xml:id="pg572"/> notice. Furnish all United States and British vessels of
                    war and revenue cutters with lists of vessels warned. Remain in neighborhood of
                    Sand Point until receipt of further instructions, which will be sent by <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marion</hi>. Receive on board and transport to Sand
                    Point, C. H. Bullard, deputy collector of customs, but do not delay sailing on
                    his account.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tracy</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
